  {
    "number": 104,
    "title": "docs: add BUNNY HTML system design",
    "body": "BUNNY's architecture is spread across contracts, ADRs and implementation issues. Add a linked HTML design set with an overview, 26 component documents, a combined reading/print view and an interactive state/action diagram. The pages separate delivered source from planned modules and qualification work, and trace agent observations, music updates, explicit commands and device execution.\n\nEditable HTML fragments and a JSON inventory generate the reading pages. The UI includes searchable navigation, dark/light themes, mobile layouts and print styles. The inventory records the composable template provenance and pinned repository sources. This is documentation and document-assembly tooling; no product behavior or OpenSpec capability changes, deployment, installation or device access.\n\nRefs #103.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Node 24 setup and workflow checks pass: four specifications, four archives and 15 workflow tests.\n- Document generation and validation pass: 28 reading pages, 1,022 local links, unique anchors, complete inventory and unchanged authored sources.\n- Browser checks pass for desktop/mobile navigation, search, themes, all component pages and print, with no page errors or external requests from the reading pages.\n- The architecture diagram passes nine checks and desktop browser containment/readability checks. Its rendered HTML is committed with the source JSON.\n- Work-guide generation, five maintenance tests and browser checks pass. The development-workflow section, issue coverage and CI/documentation timeline include #103; the nine existing guide viewers remain unchanged. Details are in `docs/work-guide/updates.md`.\n- CI retains the existing guide checks and adds deterministic document and browser validation with review artifacts. Public publication is outside this change; the public guide currency check is recorded separately.\n\nReview comparison: base/merge-base `514b566279f271451e36a5bb86b166bfa2a33bd8`, head `a9f9816f787e0c6f8b910e40c51a304babc567b9`. The worktree is clean. Independent read-only Standards and Specification reviews passed with no findings on this exact comparison. The Standards reviewer independently reran the browser checks and inspected desktop/mobile output. Explicit user approval of this HTML candidate is still required before merge.\n\nHosted CI is blocked: all 13 configured jobs were marked failed without starting any steps. Each job annotation reports failed account payments or a spending-limit restriction. See the [Checks run](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/actions/runs/35485258782) and [Work guide run](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/actions/runs/35485258902). An account owner needs to resolve that restriction, then both runs must succeed on this head. Local checks do not replace the hosted gate. No merge, issue closure, deployment or public publication is claimed.\n",
    "state": "open",
